#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:3
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:5
msgid ""
"pipx has no user configuration file. Every setting is an environment "
"variable, all of them optional. Run ``pipx environment`` to print each "
"variable as set in your environment, followed by the values pipx derives "
"from them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:8
msgid ""
"With ``pipx environment --value VARIABLE`` (or ``-V``), pipx prints the "
"value it computes for a variable that the full output lists under ``Derived "
"values``: the read-only values below, and the settable paths and flags pipx "
"resolves, such as ``PIPX_HOME`` and ``PIPX_BIN_DIR``. For any other variable "
"it prints the raw environment value, or an empty line when the variable is "
"unset, even if pipx applies a default; the tables below list each default. "
"To read what pipx applies instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:14
msgid ""
"for ``PIPX_DEFAULT_BACKEND``, query ``PIPX_RESOLVED_BACKEND``, the backend "
"new environments get;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:15
msgid ""
"for a ``PIPX_GLOBAL_*`` path outside Windows, add ``--global`` and query the "
"name without ``GLOBAL_``, for example ``pipx environment --global --value "
"PIPX_BIN_DIR`` (``--global`` does not exist on Windows)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:20
msgid "Settable variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:26
msgid "Variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:27
msgid "Meaning and default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:28
msgid "``PIPX_HOME``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:29
msgid ""
"Root directory for pipx virtual environments. Default: "
"``platformdirs.user_data_path(\"pipx\")`` — Linux ``~/.local/share/pipx``, "
"macOS ``~/Library/Application Support/pipx``, Windows ``%LOCALAPPDATA%"
"\\pipx\\pipx``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:31
msgid "``PIPX_BIN_DIR``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:32
msgid ""
"Directory for application entry-point symlinks. Default: ``~/.local/bin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:33
msgid "``PIPX_MAN_DIR``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:34
msgid "Directory for man page symlinks. Default: ``~/.local/share/man``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:35
msgid "``PIPX_COMPLETION_DIR``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:36
msgid "Directory for shell completion symlinks. Default: ``~/.local/share``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:37
msgid "``PIPX_GLOBAL_HOME``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:38
msgid ""
"Root directory for global (``--global``) virtual environments. Default: ``/"
"opt/pipx``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:39
msgid "``PIPX_GLOBAL_BIN_DIR``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:40
msgid "Entry-point directory for global installs. Default: ``/usr/local/bin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:41
msgid "``PIPX_GLOBAL_MAN_DIR``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:42
msgid ""
"Man page directory for global installs. Default: ``/usr/local/share/man``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:43
msgid "``PIPX_GLOBAL_COMPLETION_DIR``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:44
msgid ""
"Shell completion directory for global installs. Default: ``/usr/local/"
"share``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:45
msgid "``PIPX_SHARED_LIBS``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:46
msgid ""
"Override the shared libraries directory. pipx ignores it with ``--global``. "
"Default: ``$PIPX_HOME/shared``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:47
msgid "``PIPX_DEFAULT_PYTHON``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:48
msgid ""
"Python interpreter used when ``--python`` is not passed: a path, or a "
"command name (``python3.12``) or version (``3.12``) looked up on ``PATH``. "
"Default: the interpreter running pipx (``sys.executable``); on Windows, "
"unless pipx runs inside a venv, the ``py`` launcher's default Python or "
"``python`` on ``PATH``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:51
msgid "``PIPX_DEFAULT_BACKEND``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:52
msgid ""
"Backend for new venvs, ``pip`` or ``uv``. Default: ``uv`` when `uv <https://"
"docs.astral.sh/uv/>`_ 0.9.17 or newer is available, else ``pip``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:54
msgid "``PIPX_COOLDOWN``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:55
msgid ""
"Default for ``--cooldown``: ignore index artifacts uploaded fewer than this "
"many days ago, on ``install``, ``install-all``, ``inject``, ``upgrade``, "
"``upgrade-all`` and ``run``. An explicit ``--cooldown`` wins, and ``--"
"cooldown 0`` opts a single command out. A locked install ignores it. "
"Default: unset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:58
msgid "``PIPX_FETCH_PYTHON``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:59
msgid ""
"When to fetch a standalone Python build: ``always``, ``missing``, or "
"``never``. Default: ``never``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:60
msgid "``PIPX_FETCH_MISSING_PYTHON``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:61
msgid "Deprecated alias for ``PIPX_FETCH_PYTHON=missing``. Default: unset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:62
msgid "``PIPX_DISABLE_SHARED_LIBS_AUTO_UPGRADE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:63
msgid ""
"Set to a truthy value to skip automatic shared library upgrades. Default: "
"unset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:64
msgid "``PIPX_USE_EMOJI``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:65
msgid ""
"Set to ``1``, ``y``, ``yes``, ``t``, ``true``, or ``on`` (case-insensitive) "
"to force emoji output; any other value disables it. Default: enabled when "
"the stderr encoding supports the emoji glyphs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:67
msgid "``PIPX_MAX_LOGS``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:68
msgid ""
"Number of command logs to keep in the log directory, counting the current "
"command's; `pip <https://pip.pypa.io>`_ and ``uv`` error logs share a "
"separate limit of the same size. ``0`` acts like ``1``. pipx keeps the logs "
"of commands still running. Default: ``10``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:74
msgid ""
"pipx falls back to ``USE_EMOJI`` (unprefixed) when ``PIPX_USE_EMOJI`` is "
"unset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:78
msgid ""
"pipx forwards the standard ``PIP_*`` environment variables (for example "
"``PIP_INDEX_URL``) to ``pip``, except that it forces ``PIP_USER=0`` and "
"``PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1``, drops ``PIP_TARGET``, and defaults "
"``PIP_KEYRING_PROVIDER`` to ``subprocess``. See :doc:`Troubleshoot <../how-"
"to/troubleshoot>` if ``pip`` behaves unexpectedly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:84
msgid "Legacy fallback home"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:86
msgid ""
"If a legacy home directory already exists on disk, pipx keeps its virtual "
"environments there instead of the ``PIPX_HOME`` default: ``~/.local/pipx`` "
"on any platform, and ``~\\pipx`` on Windows. pipx uses them only when "
"present and when ``PIPX_HOME`` is unset. See :doc:`Configure paths <../how-"
"to/configure-paths>` to migrate off them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:90
msgid ""
"On Unix, a pipx installation that manages itself recovers ``PIPX_HOME`` and "
"``PIPX_DEFAULT_PYTHON`` from its own virtual environment when those "
"variables are unset, and ``PIPX_BIN_DIR`` when pipx was launched through its "
"exposed link, so later shells stay attached to the same installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/environment-variables.rst:94
msgid ""
"A pipx installed with ``--global`` lives in the global home "
"(``PIPX_GLOBAL_HOME``, ``/opt/pipx`` by default) and recovers only "
"``PIPX_DEFAULT_PYTHON``: without ``--global`` it uses the per-user defaults, "
"with ``--global`` the global ones. With a custom ``PIPX_GLOBAL_HOME``, every "
"user who runs that pipx must set it; otherwise pipx treats the global home "
"as their own ``PIPX_HOME``. pipx recovers ``PIPX_DEFAULT_PYTHON`` only while "
"the recorded interpreter still resolves to the one its environment runs on; "
"it ignores a record left pointing into a removed bootstrap environment and "
"falls back to its own interpreter."
msgstr ""

